      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to identify the \\(x\\)-intercept, which is the value of \\(a\\) when \\(x=0\\), and the \\(y\\)-intercepts, which are the solutions to \\(y=0\\) for both \\(x=0\\) and \\(x \\neq 0\\).\n\n1. **Finding \\(a\\):**\n    - The \\(x\\)-intercept occurs when \\(y = 0\\).\n    - Substitute \\(y = 0\\) into the equation \\(x = 2y^2 - 6y + 3\\):\n    \\begin{align*}\n    x &= 2(0)^2 - 6(0) + 3 \\\\\n    x &= 3.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Hence, \\(a = 3\\).\n\n2. **Finding \\(b\\) and \\(c\\):**\n    - The \\(y\\)-intercepts occur when \\(x = 0\\), so we solve:\n    \\begin{align*}\n    0 &= 2y^2 - 6y + 3.\n    \\end{align*}\n    The solutions to this quadratic equation are the values of \\(y\\) when \\(x = 0\\).\n\nUsing the quadratic formula \\(y = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\\):\n    - For \\(y = 2\\):\n    \\begin{align*}\n    y &= \\frac{6 \\pm \\sqrt{36 - 24}}{4} \\\\\n    y &= \\frac{6 \\pm \\sqrt{12}}{4} \\\\\n    y &= \\frac{6 \\pm 2\\sqrt{3}}{4} \\\\\n    y &= \\frac{3 \\pm \\sqrt{3}}{2.\n    \\end{align*}\n    Hence, \\(b = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\) and \\(c = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}\\).\n\n    - For \\(x \\neq 0\\), we already have one \\(y\\) value for each \\(x\\) intercept when we substitute \\(y = 0\\) into the function.\n    - We must also consider the solutions by solving:\n    \\begin{align*}\n    0 &= (y - a)(2y^2 - 6y + 3) + 3(2y - 1).\n    \\end{align*}\n    This simplifies to solving:\n    \\begin{align*}\n    0 &= (y - (a))(2y - 3)(y - 1), \\quad \\text{giving } y = a, y = \\frac{3}{2}, y = 1. f \\left(\\right.\n    \\end{align*} Values. We can read \\(b, c\\) from these.\n\nSince we have the points, solving the following calculations:\n\n    \\[ b = \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2}. \\]\n    \\[ c = \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2}. \\]\n    \\[ a = 3 \\]\n\nFinally, we sum \\( a, b, c \\):\n\n\\[\na + b + c = 3 + \\frac{3 + \\sqrt{3}}{2} + \\frac{3 - \\sqrt{3}}{2} \n\\]\n\nWe'll consolidate this in Python:\n```python\nimport sympy as sp\n\n# Define the symbols\na, b, c = 3, (3 + sp.sqrt(3))/2, (3 - sp.sqrt(3))/2\n\n# Calculate the sum of a, b, and c\nsum_abc = a + b + c\nsum_abc_simplified = sp.simplify(sum_abc)\nprint(sum_abc_simplified)\n```\n```output\n6\n```\nThe sum of \\( a \\), \\( b \\), and \\( c \\) is  \n\\[\n\\boxed{6}.\n\\]",
